# Single-instance EntKube. For two web instances plus a worker, see
# docs/running-two-instances.md and docs/examples/Caddyfile.two-instances.
#
# ⚠️ Adding a second upstream to the reverse_proxy line below is NOT enough, and the way it fails
# is silent: Caddy's default policy is `random`, so GET /_blazor?id=… reaches an instance that did
# not mint the token about half the time, and the page renders perfectly while responding to
# nothing. Sticky sessions (`lb_policy cookie`) are mandatory — a SignalR backplane does not help,
# because a Blazor Server circuit lives in one process.
{
	email {env.ACME_EMAIL}
}

{env.DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy entkube:8080
}
